/** @page ncursesreleasenotes Release Notes

    @section ncurses_1_0 ncurses Module Version 1.0
    - initial release

    Scrollable text prepares wrapping before measuring scroll limits, maps
    source positions to display cells, preserves the viewport anchor on resize,
    and clips styled Unicode text at widget boundaries. Cursor requests can be
    released without disturbing a newer request from another widget. Develop
    pipelines reuse successful platform tests for identical Git trees.

    Focus routing reaches nested controls, modal scopes preserve Tab traversal
    and restore eligible prior focus, and explicit popups support outside-click
    dismissal. Text inputs and combo boxes share grapheme-safe editing and mouse
    caret mapping. Cursor indices remain character offsets; partial replacement
    ranges expand to whole graphemes. Session::setCursor() now returns the prior
    visibility so modal transitions can restore it exactly. Composite file-browser
    pane navigation stays synchronized with managed focus, and combo-box mouse
    placement and dropdown scrolling share the clipped drawing geometry.
    Composite mouse delegation preserves panel-local coordinate conversion and
    preview navigation. Focus callbacks share a thread-local transition guard,
    including cleanup triggered by hiding, disabling, and detaching widgets.
*/
